<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import DealSheet from './lib/DealSheet.abide'
import dealSheet from './lib/DealSheet.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import FilterDrawer from './lib/FilterDrawer.abide'
import filterDrawer from './lib/FilterDrawer.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import GrabberDragged from './lib/GrabberDragged.abide'
import grabberDragged from './lib/GrabberDragged.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/dialog', '/headless/resizable']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealPanel.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the deal panel opens from the edge and sizes from its handle'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/drawer.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a drawer opens as its dialog does",
                "test(\"a drawer's backdrop is its dialog's",
                "test('a drawer with stops let go settles at the nearest stop",
                "test('a drawer with no stops let go rests where it was dropped",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Open filters from the side of the page">
        <p>A drawer is a <code>dialog</code> with a <code>resizable</code>'s panel laid over it.
            Spread <code>drawer</code> on a <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> and
            <code>handle</code> on its inner edge. It opens, closes and dismisses as a dialog
            does, its handle sizes it as a resizable's does, and <code>data-side</code> tells
            your CSS which edge it stands on.</p>
        <Example code={filterDrawer}><FilterDrawer /></Example>
    </Section>
    <Section level={3} title="Raise a list of deals from the bottom on a phone">
        <p>Give <code>stops</code>, sizes as shares of the viewport across its edge, and a
            drawer let go settles at the nearest one, a flick carrying it on to the next.
            Dragged below every stop, it closes. Without <code>stops</code> it rests where it
            is dropped. Give <code>modal: false</code> to keep the page behind it usable.</p>
        <Example code={dealSheet}><DealSheet /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Widen the grabber while the sheet is dragged">
        <p>The handle carries <code>data-dragging</code> from the press to the release.</p>
        <Example code={grabberDragged}><GrabberDragged /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
